<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Nightly promote-or-hold pass over the fleet-alert bucket (ASK-1133).
     TEMPLATE, not a loadable plist: __KIPI_REPO__ and __HOME__ are materialized by
     install-plist.sh, the convention com.kipi.linear-dor uses (ASK-113 / ASK-191).
     Install: bash q-system/.q-system/scripts/install-plist.sh com.kipi.linear-alert-triage

     WHY IT EXISTS (PR #268 R1). The lane without a scheduled caller is the defect
     the script was written to fix: a consumer nothing invokes.

     COMMITTED IS NOT INSTALLED. `kipi install-jobs` picks this up with no
     registration, from the PRIMARY checkout only, and nothing runs install-jobs
     automatically yet. ASK-1130 owns that gap for every kipi job.

     FLEET-WIDE ON PURPOSE (R5): no project flag. The script refuses one on `run`.

     02:30, half an hour AHEAD of com.kipi.linear-dor at 03:00: a promoted ticket
     already carries a DoR, so the drafter skips it instead of spending a slot.

     stdout goes to .log, not .out: .out is the run-evidence file the script itself
     appends one line to per pass, and pointing stdout there would double it.

     PATH IS SET HERE BECAUSE `bash -lc` DID NOT SET IT (ASK-3823). A bash login
     shell reads ~/.profile, and ~/.local/bin, where claude is installed, reaches
     PATH only through ~/.zshrc. 15 passes logged "0 written, 8 failed" with
     "no working claude binary" on every row. /etc/profile's path_helper puts
     the system dirs first and keeps these entries after them (measured), so
     claude, gh and python3 all resolve.

     USER AND LOGNAME TOO, OR CLAUDE IS FOUND AND STILL FAILS (PR #628 R1). The
     claude login lives in the keychain, and the lookup needs them: without them
     `claude -p` answers "Not logged in", rc 1, on every row (ASK-1178 measured the
     same 2026-08-30). launchd's default environment for this job is PATH alone.
     Same four keys as com.kipi.weekly-improve. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.kipi.linear-alert-triage</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string><string>-lc</string>
    <string>cd __KIPI_REPO__ &amp;&amp; ./kipi alert-triage run --limit 8 --apply</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key><dict><key>Hour</key><integer>2</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>HOME</key><string>__HOME__</string>
    <key>USER</key><string>__USER__</string>
    <key>LOGNAME</key><string>__USER__</string>
    <key>PATH</key><string>__HOME__/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__HOME__/.config/kipi/linear-alert-triage.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__HOME__/.config/kipi/linear-alert-triage.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
